exit: 1
-- CAPABILITY --------------- errors/cap_mismatch_3.march

`tidy` needs file-system access, but `fr` is the file-read capability. [cap_mismatch]

14 |     let _ = tidy(fr, "/tmp/x")
                      ^^

    `IO.FileRead` is a part of `IO.FileSystem`; it does not carry the rest of `IO.FileSystem`.
    help: give `main` a `Cap(IO.FileSystem)` parameter and pass it to `tidy`.

    `tidy` needs `Cap(IO.FileSystem)`:

14 |     let _ = tidy(fr, "/tmp/x")
                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `fr` was bound here as `Cap(IO.FileRead)`:

13 |   fn main(fr : Cap(IO.FileRead)) do
               ^^

    `main` is granted only `Cap(IO.FileRead)` here:

13 |   fn main(fr : Cap(IO.FileRead)) do
              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

13 -   fn main(fr : Cap(IO.FileRead)) do
13 +   fn main(fr : Cap(IO.FileRead), _cap_filesystem : Cap(IO.FileSystem)) do
14 -     let _ = tidy(fr, "/tmp/x")
14 +     let _ = tidy(_cap_filesystem, "/tmp/x")



after fix: exit 0
